    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine will rely heavily on **Kyle Tucker** today, who carries the slate\u2019s elite score of 69.61. He faces a favorable matchup against a pedestrian 4.07 xERA arm, providing the high-floor, high-ceiling profile we need to anchor the outfield. While the overall lineup depth is tested by a difficult assignment against Chase Burns\u2014who suppresses production with a 3.01 xERA\u2014**Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a primary target at 55.84. Even against a tough pitcher, his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and premium spot in the #2 hole elevate him above the marginal tier, making him our second most valuable asset for the day.\n\nWe are navigating a treacherous pitching slate, which forced several high-floor players into the \"marginal\" 40\u201359 range. **Andy Pages** (57.86) is the most notable of these, nearly eclipsing the 60-point threshold despite the small penalty for an elite opposing backstop. The most difficult bench decision involved **Heliot Ramos**, who scraped a 41.12 score but ultimately fell behind the rest of the utility mix due to the severe SP skill penalty (-19%) against the Sheehan matchup. Our depth is further constrained by the scheduled rest for stalwarts like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who are not in action today, leaving us to lean on the likes of **Nasim Nunez** and **Dominic Smith** to fill the gaps. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining on the IL, we are focused on managing game caps carefully while waiting for the return of **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Josh Lowe** to restore our full offensive ceiling.",
